 ALE IDOCS
 ---------
 It will help to transfer the data from one system to another system

 Idoc structure  :
 -----------------
 1. Control Record
 It consists of receiver information, sender information, port information and RFC connection information
 2. Data record
 It consists of Actual data which we are transferring from one system to another system
 3. Status record
 It consists of status of Idoc whether it is which status failed or success or in process

 Tables :
 -------
 1. Control date-EDIDC
 2. Data record ---EDID4
 3. Status record-EDIDS

 Standard basic types:
 ---------------------
 Customer master: DEBMAS06
 Material master: MATMAS03
 Orders: ORDERSOS
 Delivery: DELVRY01
 Invoice: INVOIC02
 Vendor: CREMAS05
 Accounting doc: FIDCCP02

 Standard Message types :
 -----------------------
 Customer master: DEBMAS
 Material master: MATMAS
 PO to Orders: ORDERS.
 Order to PO: ORDRSP
 Delivery: DESADV
 Invoice: INVOIC
 Vendor: CREMAS

 Inbound Idoc message number :
 -----------------------------
 50-Idoc Added
 64-Ready to proceed
 62-Idoc passed application
 53-IDOC successfully updated
 51-Idoc failed
 69-edit and ready to process
 68-Idoc deleted

 Outbound Idoc message numbers :
 ------------------------------
 01-Idoc generated
 30-Ready to proceed
 03-Idoc successful
 02-Idoc failed

 Configuration
 --------------
 1. SALE to define logical system--- Basis consultant responsible
 2. SALE-to assign logical system --- Basis consultant responsible
 3. SM59-To maintain RFC connection -- Basis consultant responsible
 4. WE21-To define PORT  --- Basis consultant responsible
 5. BD64 - To maintain distribution model -- Functional consultant responsible
 6. WE20-To generate partner profile --- Functional consultant responsible

 -> WE31-To create new segment
 -> WE30-To create new basic types
 -> WE81-To create new message types
 -> WE82-assign message type to basic types
 -> WE57-Assign functional module to message type and basic type
 -> WE41-Outbound Process code
 -> WE42-Inbound Process code

 Idoc t-codes for monitor or reprocess :
 ---------------------------------------
 1. WE19-To change the data in segment or add new segment
 2. BD87- To reprocess the IDOC
 3. WE02- To check the Idoc status
 4. WE05-To check the Idoc status
 5. WE09- To check IDOC business content
 6. BD10- To transfer material
 7. BD12-To transfer customer

